      {
        "id": "p50-q47-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac45$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sin2\\theta}{80}=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{50}$, so $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac45$.",
          "worked": "By the sine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin2\\theta}{80}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{50}\\\\\\frac{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{80}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{50}\\\\100\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta&=80\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac45.\\end{align*}$$\nDivision by $\\sin\\theta$ is valid because $\\theta$ is an interior angle of the triangle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p50-q47-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the exact area of the plot of land.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1872\\ \\mathrm{m}^2$.\n\nUse $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac35$ and $\\angle BAC=180^\\circ-3\\theta$ in the triangle-area formula.",
          "worked": "$\\theta$ is acute, so $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac35$. Also, $\\angle BAC=180^\\circ-3\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac35\\right)\\left(\\frac45\\right)=\\frac{24}{25}\\\\\\cos2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac45\\right)^2-1=\\frac7{25}\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=\\sin2\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\cos2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=\\frac{24}{25}\\cdot\\frac45+\\frac7{25}\\cdot\\frac35\\\\\\sin3\\theta&=\\frac{117}{125}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area}&=\\frac12(50)(80)\\sin(180^\\circ-3\\theta)\\\\\\text{Area}&=2000\\cdot\\frac{117}{125}\\\\\\text{Area}&=1872\\ \\mathrm{m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
